From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: saving metadata (Save, SaveEx, GetSizeMax of the writers)

IWICPersistStream::Save, SaveEx and GetSizeMax of the metadata writers returned
E_NOTIMPL, so nothing a program put into a writer could be written to a stream.

Writers now serialise to the format their readers load:
 - PNG tEXt, gAMA, cHRM, hIST and tIME as chunks (length, type, data, CRC).
 - GIF logical screen descriptor, image descriptor, graphic control extension,
   application extension and comment extension (text cut into sub-blocks).
 - IFD, Exif and GPS directories: entries sorted by tag, values that fit four bytes
   inline, the others behind the table, little or big endian (the persist option),
   nested Exif and GPS directories written after the table and pointed to.
 - App1: "Exif" and two zeros, the TIFF header, the directory.
 - Unknown metadata: its bytes.
SaveEx with clear-dirty clears the dirty state; GetSizeMax is the size Save writes;
readers still refuse (E_NOTIMPL). Helpers (a growable buffer, item lookup) are shared
by the serialisers.
